---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout
  title="News & Events"
  description="District-wide news and events across MBR City — Meydan racing, District One's lagoon calendar, and what's genuinely district-level rather than one community's."
>
  <section class="container hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">News & events</p>
    <h1>What's on, district-wide</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The distinction that matters here: this page covers what draws people
      from across MBR City's communities, not what's hyper-local to just
      one of them. For Riviera's own hyper-local calendar, see
      <a href="https://riviera.dst.llc/news-events/">its dedicated page</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>What counts as district-wide here</h2>
    <p>
      Meydan Racecourse events — most notably the Dubai World Cup — draw
      attention and traffic across the whole district, not just Meydan
      residents. District One's Crystal Lagoon hosts its own seasonal
      programming that pulls from neighbouring communities. New retail or
      infrastructure openings that change how the district functions as a
      whole belong here too — a new Meydan One Mall tenant matters
      district-wide in a way a single promenade café opening in Riviera
      doesn't.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Community-specific coverage</h2>
    <p>
      For what's happening inside one specific community rather than
      district-wide, that content lives on that community's own site where
      one exists — Riviera's <a href="https://riviera.dst.llc/news-events/">local news & events page</a>
      is the model this network follows as it covers more of MBR City's
      individual communities the same way.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero { padding-top: var(--space-5); }
  .lede { font-size: var(--step-1); color: var(--ink-muted); max-width: 65ch; }
</style>
